    "evidence_text": "Introduction\tKnowledge Base Question Answering (KBQA) systems answer questions by obtaining information from KB tuples  ,  ,  ,  ,  ,  .\n\nIn order to assess how the proposed improved relation detection could benefit the KBQA end task, we also propose a simple KBQA\n\nKBQA with two-step relation detection  Compared to previous approaches, the main difference is that we have an additional entity re-ranking step after the initial entity linking.\n\nThe KBQA end task, as a result, benefits from this process.\n\nWebQSP (WQ): A multi-relation KBQA task.\n\nKBQA systems: (1) Removing the entity re-ranking step significantly decreases the scores.\n\nConclusion\tKB relation detection is a key step in KBQA and is significantly different from general relation extraction tasks.\n\nHR-BiLSTM, that performs hierarchical matching between questions and KB relations.\n\nOur model outperforms the previous methods on KB relation detection tasks and allows our KBQA system to achieve state-of-the-arts.\n\nFor example, our model could be integrated into the decoder in  , to provide better sequence prediction.\n\nWe will also investigate new emerging datasets like GraphQuestions  and ComplexQuestions  to handle more characteristics of general QA.",
